 "intro": "Hatra, a walled Arab city in the Mesopotamian desert, 117 AD. Hatra has revolted against Trajan’s new conquests. You are the Emperor Trajan, ill and over sixty.",
 "debrief": "In Cassius Dio’s account, Trajan’s army suffered in the desert from lack of water, food and fodder. His engines made a breach, but the cavalry sent in was thrown back. Riding near the walls, Trajan was recognised by his grey hair and nearly hit; a cavalryman beside him was killed. Lightning, hail and swarms of flies tormented the army, and Trajan gave up. He died on the way home, and Hadrian gave up most of the eastern conquests. The other choices are what-ifs.",
